lldpdu

parse and build IEEE 802.1AB LLDP data units

USAGE

     use lldpdu::{frame, ChassisId, Lldpdu, PortId};

     let payload = frame::lldpdu_of(&captured)?;
     let pdu = Lldpdu::parse(payload)?;

DESCRIPTION

     lldpdu reads and writes LLDP data units as defined in IEEE 802.1AB-2016.
     Depends on the Rust standard prelude.
     The crate is no_std.
     The parser itself borrows from the input and doesn't make copies.

LAYOUT

     tlv      raw type/length/value layer: TlvIter, encoder, type
              constants (§8.4.1)

     types    typed vocabulary: ChassisId, PortId, SystemCapabilities,
              ManagementAddress, OrgTlv (§8.5–8.6)

     pdu      Lldpdu, a complete data unit, parsed or under construction
              (§8.2)

     frame    Ethernet demux: EtherType 0x88CC, the three group
              addresses, lldpdu_of (§7.1)

SEE ALSO

     IEEE Std 802.1AB-2016

